================================================================================
## Paged Stage-3 completion — fix ontology Generate truncation loop (issue #173)
================================================================================

Context: GitHub issue #173 — Ontology Generate failed with the
"ontology output is truncated. Retrying…" loop whenever a completion
substage's full answer could not fit the endpoint's ~8k-token output cap:
100+ tables × 15-20 columns, a single 360/164-column table, or a large
attached document. Each substage asked for its ENTIRE JSON in one call; a
length-capped answer got one hopeless "re-emit concisely" retry and then
failed the whole run. Fixed per the maintainer-scoped design on the issue:
bound each completion pass (pages), never one-shot the full output.

Changes:

1. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py`
   `build_{relations,attributes,axioms}_response_format` now require a
   `has_more` boolean page flag (strict schema: in `properties` AND
   `required`); `parse_*_payload` returns `has_more` via the new
   `_coerce_has_more` (missing field → False = single-page back-compat,
   stray "true"/"false" strings coerced like the double-encoding quirk).
2. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
   New `_PAGINATION_RULE` block shared by the three completion system
   prompts (bounded complete-item pages, `has_more` semantics); output
   examples now show `"has_more": false`; new
   `build_continuation_user_prompt` (next page) and
   `build_truncated_page_retry_prompt` (same page, fewer items).
3. `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
   `_run_completion` is now a bounded paging loop instead of one call +
   one concise-reemit retry: merges/dedupes pages per substage key_fn,
   stops when `has_more` is false or a page adds zero new items, one
   smaller-page retry on `finish_reason=length`, clear failure past
   `_MAX_COMPLETION_PAGES` (16, `options["max_completion_pages"]`).
   Schema validation + entity-closure `validate_references` run on every
   page — reject-only unchanged. Extracted module helpers
   `_call_completion_page`, `_accept_completion_page`,
   `_completion_failure`, `_queue_truncation_retry`, `_queue_next_page`
   (function-size baseline kept shrink-only: `_run_completion` is 118 LOC
   vs the 119 baseline). Relations finalize via `drop_inverse_relations`
   and axioms via `drop_multi_parent_subclass_axioms` over the merged set
   so cross-page restatements collapse.
4. `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
   New `TestCompletionPagination` (11 tests): page merge, cross-page
   dedupe, continuation message, zero-new-items stop, page-budget
   failure, truncated-page retry/failure, per-page closure rejection,
   semantic dedupe across relation pages, missing-`has_more` back-compat,
   `has_more` required in the strict schema.
5. `tests/eval/staged_contract.py`
   New `paged_completion` constraint kind (`_c_paged_completion`) driving
   scripted multi-page `infer_*` runs with `success|failure|rejected`
   outcomes — deterministic, no live endpoint.
6. `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl` and
   `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl`
   10 new `staged-paged-*` rows (kept byte-identical per the mirror test).
7. `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`
   `_MIN_STAGED_EXAMPLES` 31 → 41; `paged_completion` added to
   `_REQUIRED_STAGED_CONSTRAINT_KINDS` so the coverage cannot silently
   disappear.
8. `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md`
   §2 `max_completion_pages` identity row, §3a "Paged completion output"
   contract, §5 `stage_paged_completion` dimension, §6 failure-mode row.

Not changed (deliberately): Stage-1 detection (output already bounded by
the 40-candidate cap), checkpoint granularity (still substage-level —
a page-level failure re-runs the substage), and `run_completion`'s
merge/persistence contract (merged result shape unchanged).

Modified files:
- `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/schemas.py`
- `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/prompts.py`
- `src/agents/agent_owl_generator/staged.py`
- `tests/units/agents/test_owl_generator_staged.py`
- `tests/eval/staged_contract.py`
- `tests/eval/datasets/agent_owl_generator/baseline.jsonl`
- `tests/eval/run_agent_owl_generator.py`
- `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/SPEC.md`
- `.planning/agents/agent_owl_generator/eval/dataset.jsonl`

Tests:
- Touched-area suites: test_owl_generator_staged (75), test_owl_generator_schemas,
  test_generate_workflow, test_generate_draft, test_generate_routes,
  test_v090_generate_workflow, tests/eval/ (incl. 10 new staged-paged rows),
  tests/units/architecture — all green.
- Full routine: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 9,480 passed,
  338 skipped, 21 failed, 14 errors. All failures are pre-existing
  Windows-environment issues in areas untouched by this change
  (app.yaml template render, deploy rename guards, lakebase preflight/perms
  scripts, help deploy bundle, session symlink reaping, charmap decode) —
  CI runs on Ubuntu; none import agents/agent_owl_generator or the eval
  harness.
